{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":488923,"name":"OliG","username":"OliG","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/o/b4bc9f/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-11T12:02:21.271Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488923-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488923-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488923-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488923-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHi,\u003cbr\u003e\nI’m having a persistent issue with Grok Bot on Windows 10.\u003cbr\u003e\nDetails:\u003cbr\u003e\nGrok Bot version: 0.30.0 (Stable channel)\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: Windows 10\u003cbr\u003e\nThe problem started this morning after a Windows update.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat happened:\u003cbr\u003e\nAfter the Windows update, Grok Bot lost connection to the Agent Computer.\u003cbr\u003e\nI tried signing out and back in multiple times.\u003cbr\u003e\nAt some point the app showed a white screen with a black loading dot.\u003cbr\u003e\nAfter clearing local data and relaunching, my bots reappeared in the sidebar.\u003cbr\u003e\nHowever, the computer remains unreachable.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCurrent status:\u003cbr\u003e\nMy bots are visible again.\u003cbr\u003e\nI get the message: “Can’t reach Grok Bot’s Computer. Your Bots, files and logins are safe. If it doesn’t reconnect on its own, recover Grok Bot’s computer to keep the data.”\u003cbr\u003e\nWhen I click Recover, it fails with:\u003cbr\u003e\n“Recovery failed. The recovery couldn’t finish; Grok Bot’s computer may still be inaccessible. Your Bots, files and logins are safe.”\u003cbr\u003e\n“Update Agent Computer” button is grayed out.\u003cbr\u003e\nChecking for app updates also fails with a connection error (“Unable to check for updates. Check your connection and try again.”).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat I already tried:\u003cbr\u003e\nFully quitting the app + killing all processes\u003cbr\u003e\nSigning out / signing back in several times\u003cbr\u003e\nChanging DNS to 1.1.1.1 / 8.8.8.8 + flushing DNS\u003cbr\u003e\nTesting with mobile hotspot\u003cbr\u003e\nAttempting Recover (failed)\u003cbr\u003e\nClearing local AppData folder\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy bots, files and logins appear to be safe, but I cannot reconnect to the shared computer.\u003cbr\u003e\nCould you please check the status of my Agent Computer on your side and perform a manual recovery if needed?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThank you!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488923-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488923-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSteps to Reproduce:\u003cbr\u003e\n1.I performed a Windows 10 update this morning.\u003cbr\u003e\n2. After the update, Grok Bot (version 0.30.0) lost connection to the Agent Computer.\u003cbr\u003e\n3. I signed out and signed back in multiple times.\u003cbr\u003e\n4. The app sometimes showed a white screen with a black loading dot.\u003cbr\u003e\n5. After clearing the local AppData folder and relaunching, my bots reappeared in the sidebar.\u003cbr\u003e\n6.However, the computer remains unreachable.\u003cbr\u003e\n7. I get the error: “Can’t reach Grok Bot’s Computer. Your Bots, files and logins are safe…”\u003cbr\u003e\n8. Clicking Recover fails with: “Recovery failed. The recovery couldn’t finish; Grok Bot’s computer may still be inaccessible. Your Bots, files and logins are safe.”\u003cbr\u003e\n9. “Update Agent Computer” button is grayed out.\u003cbr\u003e\n10. Checking for updates also fails with a connection error.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488923-operating-system-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488923-operating-system-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488923-version-information-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488923-version-information-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 0.30.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-488923-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-488923-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-11T12:02:28.806Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":14,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":71.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171344,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-30-0-recover-failed-computer-inaccessible-after-windows-update-bots-visible","display_username":"OliG","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":137314,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-30-0-recover-failed-computer-inaccessible-after-windows-update-bots-visible/171344/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":489484,"name":"OliG","username":"OliG","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/o/b4bc9f/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-12T11:28:00.238Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eUpdate:\u003cbr\u003e\nBoth Recover and Reset have now failed with the same error: “Recovery/Reset failed. The computer may be in a partial state.”\u003cbr\u003e\nMy bots are still visible, but the Agent Computer remains completely inaccessible.\u003cbr\u003e\nThis started after a Windows update on September 11.\u003cbr\u003e\nCould someone from the team please check and manually recover my computer?\u003cbr\u003e\nThank you.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-12T11:28:00.238Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171344,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-30-0-recover-failed-computer-inaccessible-after-windows-update-bots-visible","display_username":"OliG","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":137314,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-30-0-recover-failed-computer-inaccessible-after-windows-update-bots-visible/171344/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":489858,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-13T08:22:06.381Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/olig\"\u003e@OliG\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSorry to hear about this! Please restart Grok Bot and let us know if it’s fixed now.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-13T08:22:06.381Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171344,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-30-0-recover-failed-computer-inaccessible-after-windows-update-bots-visible","display_username":"Colin","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Community Support Engineer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":87436,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-30-0-recover-failed-computer-inaccessible-after-windows-update-bots-visible/171344/8","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":490126,"name":"OliG","username":"OliG","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/o/b4bc9f/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-13T15:19:27.567Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/colin\"\u003e@Colin\u003c/a\u003e, I tried but the issue remains. Anything else I can do?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-14T12:34:47.812Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":8,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171344,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-30-0-recover-failed-computer-inaccessible-after-windows-update-bots-visible","display_username":"OliG","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":87436,"username":"Colin","name":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":137314,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-30-0-recover-failed-computer-inaccessible-after-windows-update-bots-visible/171344/9","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":491033,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-14T16:09:45.352Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/olig\"\u003e@OliG\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for trying that.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour Grok Bot computer is healthy on our side, so the next step is to find out what is blocking the app on your PC. The current Grok Bot version has a built-in connection checker that will tell us exactly that.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit Grok Bot\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/download/bot\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eCursor · Download Grok Bot\u003c/a\u003e and download the Windows installer.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRun the installer. It replaces your current version; your Bots, files and logins are kept.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot. If a screen says “Grok Bot is having trouble connecting”, click “Open Network Debugger” and skip to step 6.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOtherwise click your account name at the bottom of the left sidebar and choose Settings (or press Ctrl+,). In the General tab, scroll down to the System section and click “Network Debugger”.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWait for the checks to finish, then click “Details” so every line is expanded.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTake a screenshot of the whole list and post it here (or copy the lines that are red or orange). The lines that matter most start with “Api tls”, “Api unary”, “Computer tls” and “Updates feed”.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne more thing that would help: if you have an antivirus or security suite installed (Kaspersky, Avast, AVG, Bitdefender, Norton, ESET, McAfee…), please tell us which one!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":16,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-14T16:09:45.352Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171344,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-30-0-recover-failed-computer-inaccessible-after-windows-update-bots-visible","display_username":"Colin","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://cursor.com/download/bot","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Cursor · Download Grok Bot","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"Community Support Engineer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":87436,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-30-0-recover-failed-computer-inaccessible-after-windows-update-bots-visible/171344/16","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":491100,"name":"OliG","username":"OliG","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/o/b4bc9f/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-14T17:42:02.329Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/colin\"\u003e@Colin\u003c/a\u003e, please find attached the required screenshots. Regarding the antivirus, I am using Kaspersky.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMany Thanks.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/f/7/f700787df9519dc00b51266e8025e90d6df362cb.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/zf4Wvf2bxbFShCCsK6nRKu5ZiZl.png?dl=1\" title=\"image\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/f/7/f700787df9519dc00b51266e8025e90d6df362cb.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"zf4Wvf2bxbFShCCsK6nRKu5ZiZl\" width=\"690\" height=\"379\" data-dominant-color=\"E5E4E4\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eimage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e717×394 11.2 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\